                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_38\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix changes `AbstractFile.onModification()` so that `validatePath()` is only\ninvoked when the `application.filesystem.unique.paths` config switch\n(`validatePathUniqueness`) is enabled:\n\n    boolean valid = true;\n    if (validatePathUniqueness) {\n        valid = validatePath(securityContext, errorBuffer);\n    }\n    return valid && super.onModification(...);\n\ninstead of the previous, unconditional:\n\n    final boolean valid = validatePath(securityContext, errorBuffer);\n    return valid && super.onModification(...);\n\nTracing the history of `AbstractFile.java`:\n\n- candidate_33 introduced the `validatePathUniqueness` static flag (read from\n  `Services.APPLICATION_FILESYSTEM_UNIQUE_PATHS`) and put the actual gating\n  logic *inside* `validatePath()` itself:\n      public boolean validatePath(...) {\n          if (validatePathUniqueness) {\n              ... uniqueness check ...\n          }\n          return true;\n      }\n  At this point both `onCreation` and `onModification` called `validatePath()`\n  unconditionally, but since the config check lived inside `validatePath()`,\n  the switch was still correctly respected everywhere.\n\n- candidate_38 refactored `onCreation` to introduce\n  `validateAndRenameFileOnce()` and wrapped that call with\n  `if (validatePathUniqueness) { ... }` \u2014 but at the same time it REMOVED the\n  `if (validatePathUniqueness)` guard from inside `validatePath()` itself\n  (the uniqueness-check code now runs unconditionally whenever\n  `validatePath()` is called). It did NOT touch `onModification()`, which\n  still directly calls `validatePath(securityContext, errorBuffer)` without\n  any surrounding guard. As a result, from this commit onward, renaming/\n  modifying a file always ran the uniqueness validation regardless of the\n  `application.filesystem.unique.paths` setting, while file *creation*\n  correctly respected the switch (via the new guarded\n  `validateAndRenameFileOnce` call). This exact asymmetry \u2014 creation respects\n  the switch, modification/renaming does not \u2014 is precisely what the fix\n  commit corrects by adding the missing `if (validatePathUniqueness)` guard\n  around the `validatePath()` call in `onModification()`.\n\nLater candidates (candidate_34, candidate_36) only changed the method\nsignature of `onModification` (adding `ModificationQueue`) or unrelated\n`isValid` logic, without altering this behavior, so the bug persisted\nunchanged from candidate_38 until it was fixed in the actual fix commit\n(candidate_40 in this list is in fact identical to the fix diff itself, i.e.\nthe resolution \u2014 not the introduction \u2014 of the bug).\n"
